**On Codex.** Agreed, and it fits the gentle-burn rule from the eighth. The four Claude lanes are not resumed. Their handoffs are written in their own hands and become Codex briefs directly: the join red first, then the Host half of PROTOCOL-61, the activity and hole generators, and the cv backlog. Codex workers would run in their own hbox worktrees under the same lane rules and the same landing script, and the judge needs no Claude at all. I stay as the director: read each landing's decision text and the convergence verdicts, rule on pause items, and brief the next wave.

