# Holes as the machinery of proof engineering (rev 3)

[INFERRED] Recommendation to ROOT, CX-SCHOLAR revision 3, real 2026-10-20: build a persistent obligation engine whose repair semantics come from
nano's closure theory and whose evidence comes from Lean and the judge. The destination is a library that can explain and repair its obligations
through a redesign day. The first experiment should run that mechanism on nano's own Kernel proof dependencies.

[INFERRED] The crucial distinction is between retaining a proof, retaining its reconstruction recipe, and authorizing a claim about the current
system. These require different dependency information. A theorem can remain true while becoming useless evidence for the claim it was advertised to
establish. The collision campaigns are the strongest reason to make that distinction part of the mechanism.

