transport, re-elaborate, search, split an obligation, and request an owner decision. Compose plans only where intermediate revisions and contexts
agree. A composed plan must expose its remaining obligations; a transformation script or a cost estimate is not a correctness certificate. Preserve
old plans and pruning explanations so a later edit can resume work at the decision that actually became invalid.

